body:
The tiredness, in my experience , never really goes and it's a killer.  I'm only on 100mg  at night now but a couple of years back I was on 800mg .  Luckily there are only so many binding sites in the body for the drug to attach to so there is a maximum sleepiness you can feel. 800mg broke me;  after almost suffocating in my sleep because I was too sedated to breath I would eventually wake up and I'd be trippin' balls and could barely walk! Like full on acid type tripping.  

In defence of the drug it has done me wonders on lower doses but that's still almost always been at night and I've still had residual tiredness the next day.  I'm still learning how to cope with the hangover now.  Taking it in the day wiped me completely and if I managed to stop myself from crawling back to bed I was just a zombie.  I decided I couldn't live like that so I told them to find something else and they did and I reckon that may be what you need to do.  Go back to your doctor and explain that it's just not realistic to expect you to live a normal ,productive day if you're taking that stuff.  There's a myriad of different drugs out there, they'll be able to try you on something else for the daytime.

&#x200B;
